# TODO - Behavioural test harness

## Objective

Create reusable tests for observable game behaviour.

## Acceptance

- Use public inputs, seeded scenarios, replays and property tests.
- Check fixed-step simulation independently of rendering frame rate.
- Do not freeze private implementation or incidental constants.
- Update contracts and tests together for intentional gameplay changes.

## Evidence

On 2026-11-24, fresh `cargo validate --no-cache` passed. The engine
now exposes reusable `InputScript`, `InputStep` and `Scripted` public-action
contracts, composed with the canonical `StepClock`. Tests use a fixed-seed
synthetic input generator and replay each recorded scenario across a
one-millisecond render schedule and independently generated frame partitions.
Property checks cover 128 seeds and compare observable state, not private
implementation constants. Focused tests protect per-tick action order, idle
ticks, correct public state updates and bounded fixed-step catch-up.

This harness contains no original game data and makes no gameplay-parity
claim. Title-specific behavioural examples will be added when owner-supplied
reference files and observable outcomes become available. Intentional
gameplay changes should update title contracts and fixtures together.
